# weld: spot welding at the bench (decisions C17, C18). A ceramic disc
# (C1) in the vise on the turntable; arm A brings a second disc's lead
# to C1's lead 2 and pincer P1 grips it there; A brings the LED (D1, a
# semiconductor) to C1's lead 1 and pincer P2 grips the LED's lead
# between its body and the lap -- a grounding clip, so the discharge's
# transient cannot reach the LED. The turntable presents each lap to
# the welder station S3, below the work, which welds it; the pincers
# let go and the three stay in the vise as one, welded.
reset circuit=weld
tool A tweezers
pick A C1 grasp=body
place A C1 at=0,0,-20
vise close
release A C1
pick A C2 grasp=body
lift A mm=80
move A to=20.08,0,-5.746
align A C2.1.tip to=C1.2.6 gap=0.1
pinch P1 on=C2.1 at=6
release A C2
lift A mm=40
pick A D1 grasp=body
lift A mm=80
move A to=-16.27,0,3.554
align A D1.1.tip to=C1.1.6 gap=0.1
pinch P2 on=D1.1 at=8
release A D1
lift A mm=60
present C1.2+C2.1 at=S3
weld S3 at=C1.2+C2.1 energy=8
present C1.1+D1.1 at=S3
weld S3 at=C1.1+D1.1 energy=8
inspect C1.1+D1.1
unpinch P1
unpinch P2
